## Download Data button 404s — DownloadPersonalData page never scaffolded

### Status
Implemented.

### GitHub Issue
#107

### Summary
`PersonalData.cshtml`'s "Download Data" button posts to `DownloadPersonalData`, a Razor
page that was never scaffolded. Clicking it always 404s.

### Reported Behavior
Found during an audit of the delete-personal-data/delete-account flow, not user-reported.
`PersonalData.cshtml:8-11` and `ManageNavPages.cs:38,86` already anticipate this page
(comment + unused nav-class helper) but no `DownloadPersonalData.cshtml(.cs)` exists under
`Areas/Identity/Pages/Account/Manage/`.

### Expected Behavior
Clicking Download Data downloads a file containing the user's stored personal data.

### Root Cause
- `PersonalData.cshtml:20` renders `<form asp-page="DownloadPersonalData" method="post">`.
- No matching page model exists, so the form 404s on submit.
- Same class of gap as `BUGS-missing-email-confirmation-pages.ospec` — a page anticipated
  by the default Identity scaffolding that was never added in this repo's pass.
- Note: none of `ApplicationUser`'s custom properties (`DisplayName`, `Color`, `CreatedAt`,
  `LastActiveAt`) are marked `[PersonalData]`, so the default scaffolded implementation
  (which reflects over `[PersonalData]`-attributed properties) would only report base
  `IdentityUser` fields (username, email, phone) unless that's addressed too — worth a
  decision before implementing, not assumed here.

### Proposed Fix
1. Scaffold `Areas/Identity/Pages/Account/Manage/DownloadPersonalData.cshtml(.cs)` in the
   generator's default style (reflect over `[PersonalData]`-attributed properties, serialize
   to JSON, return as a file download), matching CODING_CONVENTIONS.md.
2. Decide, with the developer, whether `ApplicationUser.DisplayName` (and any other custom
   field) should be marked `[PersonalData]` so it's actually included in the export.
3. Add tests exercising the actual download (not just that the button exists).

### Acceptance Criteria
- Clicking Download Data returns a file, not a 404.
- The exported data includes at least the base Identity personal-data fields.
- Tests cover the download flow.

### Out of Scope
- The separate missing-page gap already tracked in
  `Spec/Bugs/BUGS-missing-email-confirmation-pages.ospec`.
